357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 746 0 R
/E (Compressing verbose CoT into a sequence of dense latent tokens drastically reduces KV-cache pressure and accelerates generation speed.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 747 0 R
/E (Decoupling logical planning from syntactic token generation, the architecture prevents minor grammatical, or vocabulary slips from derailing the reasoning trajectory)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 748 0 R
/E (Enables gradient-based optimization of reasoning trajectories. unlike discrete token search, which requires reinforcement learning or beam search)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 749 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 750 0 R
/E (Latent prediction for structured dynamics are no longer speculative. V-JEPA 2 demonstrated that an autoregressive predictor can learn transition dynamics between compact latent states when conditioned on a frozen encoder's context. Reasoning steps are a natural candidate for the same treatment.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 751 0 R
/E (Training data is no longer the bottleneck. High-quality explicit reasoning traces with clear step structure \(DeepSeek-R1, Magpie-Reasoning\) are now plentiful, open-source, and parseable into the step-level format our approach requires.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
